  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0 (branch cut from upstream/main at 0757563d).\n\n## What changed\n\n- New `crates/ui/src/shortcut_keys.rs`: `command_key()` returns `Cmd` on macOS and `Ctrl` elsewhere (`cfg!(target_os = \"macos\")`); `chord(\"Shift+O\")` builds `Cmd+Shift+O` or `Ctrl+Shift+O`.\n- Command-shortcut hints now go through `chord`: ribbon tips in `panes.rs` (`tip_of`: New, Open, Open project, Save, Save as, Post, Undo, Redo), the operation bar hints in `op_page.rs` (Apply, Clear toolpath, Delete), the machine-cell hover in `machines_pane.rs`, and the cleared-toolpath status in `state.rs`.\n- The click-to-add pick hints go through `command_key()` / `chord` too (review fix): `geo_page.rs` `edge_hint()` (was the const `EDGE_HINT`) and `click_selects_hint()`, and `boundary.rs` `hints()` (was the const `HINTS`). The picks read `mods.command` (`edge_pick.rs`, `interact.rs`, `feature_click.rs`, #1238), so on macOS the add key is Cmd. The bindings are unchanged.\n- `command_key_for(macos: bool)`: pure form of `command_key()`, so both answers are tested on any host.\n- `gcode_view.rs` Ctrl+C is a code comment only; there is no user-visible hint string for it, so nothing changed there.\n- Structural tip-table test (`tips_match_the_imgui_table`) now asserts through `chord`, not literals, so it passes on every OS.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1239-cmd-hints.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `egui_app::tests::tips_match_the_imgui_table` (structural, tip strings for New/Open/Save/Post/Undo/Redo via `chord`)\n- `shortcut_keys::tests::command_key_names_the_platform_key` (`Cmd` under macOS cfg, `Ctrl` otherwise)\n- `shortcut_keys::tests::chord_prefixes_the_platform_key`\n- `shortcut_keys::tests::command_key_for_names_both_platforms` (`Cmd`/`Ctrl` on every host)\n- `shortcut_keys::tests::pick_hints_name_the_command_key` (edge hint, \"Click selects\" hover, boundary pick help)\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib -- --test-threads=1` from `crates/ui` (after merging upstream/main, head 415b2bd7): 620 passed, 0 failed, 5 ignored (includes the pinning tests above).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test feedback` from `crates/ui`: 6 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- PNG snapshots untouched.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The Windows/Linux branch (`Ctrl`) ran only through `command_key_for(false)` and the cfg-independent assertions; this Mac is macOS, so the `Cmd` branch is what the run covered.\n- No headless run of the app to see the hover text on screen; the strings are asserted, not painted.\n- No change to any key binding (out of scope).\n\nChangelog: Shortcut hints name Cmd on macOS (Ctrl elsewhere) instead of Ctrl for command shortcuts (#1239, PR #1293)\n\nFixes #1239\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
